<description>&lt;p&gt;Libyan armed forces continue extrajudicial executions, breaking a 15‑year moratorium, while eastern authorities carry out further killings and hold dozens of detainees at risk of execution. Haftar's forces have signed a strategic cooperation protocol with Niger and an armed group has shut down the Hamada pipeline valve, halting crude supplies to the Al-Zawiya refinery. A RPG shell caused a factory blast in Sebha that killed two people, and Jordan and Libya discussed joint military training and defense expertise exchange. Israel plans a naval blockade of Beirut and Tripoli if Hezbollah joins the conflict, and there were two battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;DW.com&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijwFBVV95cUxOSVJTNGdtNXpmTFVYUkh4N0FDbGNXVHNjQzFhb2hFYm85dzAxYWEzYUZFVEs1bGVVZkFEYVBoZ2xOM29UbFkzSGpMVVRlWVBOQUd4SzVsckpIQlN0UlBILUtJZTZDU2pkVS1SaHNzMHZ5bE1aY3NGampyNUprUkMwZGNkWWlyQjJxOS1HV3lPYw?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Libya Observer&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMickFVX3lxTFBEUTQ2YXZKUklMSGdEal9oZjVMeDg1ZjhZVXFqWmVIZFYtVDZST01aLVBfektWcEJob0ZCYVVKZzZqWFRkVXR6aVZhNENJM29xX2gtZGU3WFlRWWgyalMzV2lEVlZ3dzFyYlRyeFRHeHhwZw?oc=5&quot;&gt;Open Doors UK &amp;amp; Ireland&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwwFBVV95cUxQcVBBbmNtODlXYkpRWkxDaE1yTFlySzVVR2NNazZpM1BBalYyY3IwRm9TNlptMXJSTnM1NFRKWDlNdUJPbWtQYTJmM3dRbThFeTdfQzNhTzloY2I3LVVBeENqQlM0Z1RzdkNnZklUcENiODh3Z0NjTVFyb2JSU0ZRSERXSTAzVGQyTGlZOEZSbk5KT3BKZXBVczFyMFRpVzNlaERGN2l3WmNtWGVUMURrSHFCbnU1dzRfLXVZcm8yS19CZlk?oc=5&quot;&gt;Libya Update News - Libya Update News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMijgFBVV95cUxNU0pHamVwSnk2N0F2X1dUQmJDd3JUYnhaS01icEt0VUFNaktpVHZNSzVtbjFKbDlW